  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "A researcher named Eric Weinstein says that in the 1990s, he and a colleague, Pia Malaney, worked on applying gauge theory, a branch of mathematics from physics, to economics. He says the idea was badly received by Harvard's economics department, especially by its chairman, Dale Jorgenson, and he tells it as an example of how established institutions push back against new ideas."
